  "body": "Extend the machine definition format (`.mch`), parser, validator, and post mirror to describe an XYZAC trunnion table machine without controller RTCP.\n\n### Context\n- `parse_mch` in `crates/post/src/machine/parse.rs` flattens `kinematics.default.parts` sorted by `ctrl_coord`. That flatten step drops parent-child rotary nesting order.\n- `AxisLimits` in `crates/post/src/machine/def.rs` holds `nose_to_axis` and `axis_to_table`, not rotary `pivot`, child `offset`, `zero_offset`, or `rollover` settings.\n- `crates/post/src/post/machine.rs` derives `machine.rtcp = true` whenever any rotary tilts off Z. A Mach4 AC table tilts the work, yet the controller runs no `G43.4`.\n\n### Requirements\n- Keep parent-child rotary chain order inside `Machine` without breaking existing `axes` callers.\n- Add optional `pivot: [x, y, z]`, child `offset: [dx, dy, dz]`, `zero_offset` (degrees), and `rollover` (boolean) on rotary parts, scaling lengths by file units.\n- Define one explicit rotary sign convention (`table_rh` vs `tool_rh`) so the checker and post agree.\n- Add optional `controller.rtcp` (boolean). When `false`, mirror `machine.rtcp = false` so `fanuc.cps` and `doosan-dnm.cps` refuse `G43.4`, and mirror the full rotary chain for CAM-side IK posts.\n- Keep the unstated-limit rule from `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` and validate all new fields in `crates/app/src/machine/validate.rs`.\n\nDone means: An AC trunnion `.mch` parses, validates, mirrors these fields, refuses invalid vectors or offsets by name, and makes `fanuc.cps` and `doosan-dnm.cps` refuse when `controller.rtcp` is false.\n\nPart of #1958\n",
